# Protect local state, vault, accounts and setup reruns

- Never expose, reset or commit private .env files, encryption keys, API tokens, cookie jars, passwords, auth codes, personal account details or SQLite secrets.
- Setup reruns must be idempotent, preserve private vault/database/client registrations and avoid overwriting existing values.
- Diagnostics must be read-only unless the user explicitly authorized a change. Redact tokens from logs, browser screenshots and support output.
- Browser sessions remain in the user's browser, not copied into Blossom. A local operator confirmation is not proof of valid OAuth credentials.
- A local Mac server restart, Cloudflare tunnel provisioning, website code deploy and GitHub merge are separate operations; state which were actually performed.
- Protect the localhost admin routes when published hostname exists; tests must verify no public admin escape.
